-- R27 - DURABLE THEMES block: the daily Takeaways shows each three-month MACRO sleeve theme every morning (mark, the
-- day's evidence for and against, conflicts with tactical cards); a theme is flagged only when its stop closes or a
-- named signpost fires (both Macro Takeaways digests). Replaces R24 before R24 goes in force.
-- Source: thread "Show durable themes in daily Takeaways", 20 Nov 2026; the owner's "Yeah sure pls do" to the
-- coordinator's two-part proposal (show the sleeve daily; feed Gemini's 3-month themes to the Sunday run).
-- Proposed 20 Nov 2026 05:2xZ with dash.propose_rule; apply_after = Sun 22 Nov 2026 20:00 SGT unless "oppose R27".
-- supersedes R24: when R27 goes in force, dash.decide_rules marks R24 withdrawn ("replaced by R27 before it went in force").
-- Body and title below are byte-identical to the DB row (md5 checked: body 0c1dd129..., title a56fc7c4...).
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R27' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "DURABLE THEMES block: every morning the run shows each 3-month sleeve theme with its mark, the day's evidence for and against, and tactical cards that conflict; a theme is flagged only when its stop closes or a signpost fires", "body": "DURABLE THEMES (owner's yes of 20 Nov 2026, thread \"Show durable themes in daily Takeaways\"; replaces the MACRO SLEEVE block of R24 before it goes in force). The three-month MACRO sleeve is written each Sunday evening by the scheduled task \"Macro sleeve weekly\" (docs/macro_sleeve.md in the repo). This rule makes the daily run show those themes every morning as a short block, so the 2-to-3-month views sit beside the tactical book. It is a read-and-print rule: the daily run never originates, closes, resizes or scores a sleeve card.\n\n1. READ. At the evidence step, in the same pass as the rule reads of spec v19: Google Drive search_files with query exactly `parentId = '1LLeuELL8CLpWmtcywt2DiCpJVopNgyqm' and title contains 'macro_sleeve_current'` (excludeContentSnippets true), take the latest modifiedTime, read_file_content, strip backslash escapes. No file, or a file older than 10 days: print \"DURABLE THEMES: no current sleeve file (<date of the latest copy or none>)\" and nothing more. For each OPEN or PENDING card take from its block the META line (proxy, direction, entry or ref, stop, target, horizon, opened), THESIS and SIGNPOSTS.\n\n2. MARK. Today's level of each card's proxy comes from the same source the run uses for its own cards (the market pack or the mark script's daily bars); a sleeve card is marked in its own series (the file says when that is an ETF-level series such as GOLD or CSI300). A PENDING card whose open date has passed fills at the first daily close on or after that date: print \"filled <date> <close> (implied)\" and mark from that close. R = direction x (level - entry) / (entry - stop); for a yield proxy the direction is on the yield.\n\n3. VERDICT, AND ONLY TWO OF THEM. INTACT, or BROKEN. A theme is BROKEN only when its invalidation actually happened: (a) a daily close beyond the card's stop since its fill, or (b) one of its two SIGNPOSTS met by a dated fact in today's inputs (name the datum, its source and its value against the signpost's level). Nothing else breaks a theme: not one day's adverse move, not a contrary voice, not a tactical card the other way, not a lower mark. A move toward the stop is printed as a number, never as a verdict. There is no WEAKENED, and no theme is called broken on interpretation alone.\n\n4. PRINT. A block headed \"DURABLE THEMES [3-month sleeve, weekly · <file date>]\" directly after the TRADE BOOK block, at most 200 words in all. One entry per card:\n   \"Mnn <title> · <proxy> <long/short> · entry <x> · now <x> · <+/-x.xR> · stop <x> (<distance to stop in R, e.g. 0.6R away>) · INTACT or BROKEN\"\n   then \"for: <today's strongest evidence for the theme, <=15 words, with its source>\" and \"against: <today's strongest evidence against, <=15 words, with its source, or 'nothing new'>\". A BROKEN entry adds \"broken by: stop close <date> <close>\" or \"broken by: signpost '<signpost text>' — <datum>, <source>\", and the line \"flag for Sunday review\", which the Sunday task reads.\n   Then one CONFLICTS line: every open or pending daily-book card (including ones written today) that is on the same proxy in the opposite direction, or whose stated thesis is the opposite of a theme's thesis on the same economy or factor (for example a long AUD cross against a short AUDJPY theme): \"CONFLICTS: Pnn <proxy> <dir> vs Mnn — <horizon difference in <=10 words>\", or \"CONFLICTS: none\". The daily card itself also prints \"against sleeve Mnn\" after its TREND line. A conflict is information only: it never closes, blocks or resizes either card, and R14 applies inside each book, not across them.\n   Last line: \"sleeve scorecard: \" copied from the file's SCORECARD line.\n\n5. NEVER. The daily run never writes a MACRO card, never changes the sleeve file, never closes a sleeve card (BROKEN is a flag; the Sunday run decides), never counts a sleeve card in cum R, the SCORECARD, the TESTED list, the factor count or BOOK CHECK, and never raises or lowers a daily card's p, size or EV because a theme agrees or disagrees. The block prints in both the Fable and the Opus Macro Takeaways.\n\n6. DECISION. Unchanged from the sleeve design: at 20 closed MACRO cards or on 31 August 2027, whichever is first, the weekly review reads the sleeve file's record and proposes one of: fold the sleeve into this book as a class with its own gate, keep it as a paper book, or stop it.", "rationale": "On 20 Nov 2026 the owner asked for durable 2-to-3-month themes in the daily Takeaways and said yes to showing the weekly MACRO sleeve daily rather than adding a second theme generator. R24 (proposed 16 Nov) printed the sleeve with four verdicts including WEAKENED; a daily verdict on interpretation invites churning a three-month view on noise, so this rule keeps two verdicts and breaks a theme only on its own invalidation (a stop close or a named signpost), adds the day's evidence on both sides and the conflicts with the tactical book, and covers both pipelines now that the Opus Takeaways is being re-enabled. One Drive read and a block of at most 200 words, so the 08:15 landing is not at risk.", "evidence": "Sleeve file macro_sleeve_current of 16 Nov 2026: three cards (M01 AUDJPY short, M02 EUR10Y_AAA long yield, M03 HSI short) filling at the 17 Nov close, each with a 3 ATR(20) stop and two SIGNPOSTS. The Fable Takeaways has shown none of them since, because R24 waits for the 22 Nov window.", "revert_if": "Revert if the Drive read fails on 3 or more runs in a week, if the block costs the 08:15 SGT landing on 2 or more days with no other failure to explain it, if a theme is printed BROKEN without a stop close or a named signpost datum on 2 or more days, or if a daily card is carded, sized or priced on a theme's view (the NEVER list) on 2 or more days.", "supersedes": "R24", "review_due": "2027-02-28", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
